Here is one scoring system think that I've been thinking about. I
actually coded it half-way but I misplaced the patch and it was for
3.4.0 anyway.

The normal score system is used for non-ascensions, but an ascension
has also a separate ascension score that consists of the following:

 1.  The base score is the number of turns.
 2.  Each wish used adds 5000 turns
 3.  Each artifact picked up (except for AoY + invocation stuff) adds
     1000 turns.
 4.  Each time your life is saved add 1000 turns
 5.  Each major problem fixed by god adds 500 turns
 6.  Each zap of wand of polymorph adds 300 turns
 7.  Each turn spent standing on "Elbereth" adds 10 turns
 8.  Each turn spent causing conflict adds 7 turns
 9.  Each turn spent carrying a quest artifact adds 3 turns (cumulative
     for all quest artifacts)
 10. Each turn spent invisible adds 1 turn
 11. Each turn spent displaced adds 1 turn

At the game end you get suitable bonuses for conducts kept. I haven't
really thought about these a lot.

Lowest score wins.

The above scoring system demands sizable patching for nethack source.
However, I do have another proposal for tournament use that uses the
current system:

Each entry in the tournament consists of 13 games, once in each role.
Then, entry A is ranked higher than entry B if:

 1. A includes more ascensions than B; 
 2. A has same number of ascensions as B (> 0), and the total score
    of the ascensions in A is *lower* than the total score of
    ascensions in B; or
 2. Neither A nor B has any ascensions but the total score of A is
    *higher* than the total score of B. 

